// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
// THE REQUEST SIDE OF THE CHAT COMPLETIONS CALL, AND THE PAYLOAD OF ONE STREAMED CHUNK.
//
// The section above models the answer of a non-streaming call. This models the other two shapes
// the same endpoint involves: what the caller sends, and what one event of a streamed answer
// carries. They sit together because one member of the request decides which answer shape
// arrives: `stream` false yields one OpenAiChatCompletion200Body, `stream` true yields a run of
// OpenAiChatCompletionChunkBody payloads, one JSON object per event. This module does not own the
// event framing -- extdeps.llm.openai_compat_sse owns the `data: ` line, the `[DONE]` sentinel,
// an error that arrives as a data line, and a stream that ends without the sentinel -- and it
// lists no products, engines or endpoints: the authority is the pair of ExternalAuthority anchors at
// the top of this file -- the docs page for meaning, and the vendor's generated types pinned to a
// commit and version for names, optionality and enumerated values -- whose member lists are what the
// coverage rows below declare unmodelled rather than absent (DESIGN section 3, external upstream
// decomposition).
//
// WHY A SAMPLING PARAMETER IS AN UN-EVALUATED NUMBER LEXEME, AND NEVER A FLOAT AND NEVER TEXT.
// std.float declares Float as a name with no operators and no ruled literal home -- its comment
// records that v2 refuses a float literal with infer_reason_float_literal_home_unruled -- so a request
// read that produced a Float for `temperature` would be inventing a numeric home the language has not
// ruled, and a caller that compared `temperature` as TEXT would be validating a string standing in for
// a number. The carrier is therefore `extdeps.languages.json.grammar`'s `JsonNumberLexeme`, which is
// obtained only through its checked constructor `json_number_lexeme`: a typed JSON number lexeme with
// its standing, no range check, no comparison, and nothing here re-encodes a body -- a forwarder that
// re-emits the lexeme it read sends the client's bytes back out unchanged.
//
// `JsonNumber` IS NOT THAT CARRIER AND IS NOT A TYPE A FIELD MAY BE TYPED AS: in
// `extdeps.languages.json.emit` it is one VARIANT of `JsonValue` (`JsonNumber { lexeme:
// JsonNumberLexeme }`), so `temperature: JsonNumber` would name a variant where a type is required and
// would not resolve. The lexeme is the declaration; the variant is what the parser wraps around it.
type OpenAiCompletionStop
  = StopAtString { text: String }
  | StopAtStrings { texts: List<String> }

// Both members are optional upstream -- the generated `ChatCompletionStreamOptionsParam` is a
// total=False TypedDict -- so each is its own option rather than defaulting a client's silence.
type OpenAiStreamOptions {
  // If set, an extra chunk arrives before the `[DONE]` sentinel carrying the whole request's usage,
  // with `choices` empty; other chunks carry `usage` with a null value.
  include_usage: Bool?
  // Upstream's own member: when true, streamed deltas carry an `obfuscation` field of random
  // characters that normalizes payload size as a side-channel mitigation. It is ON BY DEFAULT, so
  // omitting it is not the same as turning it off, and a forwarder that dropped it would change what
  // the server sends.
  include_obfuscation: Bool?
}

// `max_tokens` and `max_completion_tokens` are BOTH on this endpoint's request today: the generated
// types carry `max_tokens` (the older name, deprecated upstream but still accepted) and
// `max_completion_tokens`, so a read that wants "how many tokens may I get" must look at both, and
// which one a client sent is a fact the caller keeps. The Responses API's `max_output_tokens` is a
// different endpoint's member and is not borrowed in here.
//
// `stream` IS OPTIONAL, and absent is not false in the model -- it is absent. The generated types carry
// it as two overloads, `Optional[Literal[False]]` for the non-streaming call and
// `Required[Literal[True]]` for the streaming one, so a client that never mentions `stream` is sending a
// perfectly valid request that would not inhabit a record whose `stream` were a bare `Bool`. A reader
// that needs a Bool reads `Absent` as "not streaming": that is the upstream meaning, stated here rather
// than defaulted silently inside a type.
type OpenAiChatCompletionRequest {
  model: String
  messages: List<OpenAiChatMessage>
  max_tokens: Int?
  max_completion_tokens: Int?
  n: Int?
  seed: Int?
  stop: OpenAiCompletionStop?
  stream: Bool?
  stream_options: OpenAiStreamOptions?
  reasoning_effort: OpenAiReasoningEffort?
  temperature: JsonNumberLexeme?
  top_p: JsonNumberLexeme?
  presence_penalty: JsonNumberLexeme?
  frequency_penalty: JsonNumberLexeme?
}

// WHY THIS IS THE SIXTH COPY OF A PAIR, WHAT IS GENERALIZED NOW, AND WHAT IS NOT (DESIGN section 6b).
// Five members of this file already carry the construction -- a wire-name table, a chain that reads it,
// an arm that keeps an unknown name whole, and a match that re-emits it: `OpenAiToolCallType`,
// `OpenAiResponsesOutputContentType`, `OpenAiResponsesOutputItemType`, `OpenAiResponsesStatus` and
// `OpenAiResponsesOutputItemStatus`. Read them rather than guessing: all five have the SAME unknown-name
// arm, `Other { raw: NonEmptyStr }`, and all five fill it straight from a `String`, so all five can put an
// empty runtime name behind a type whose name promises otherwise. That is the same defect this member had;
// my first cut patched it at this site alone, which was the wrong answer to a repeated pattern. Nor is the
// idiom local to this module: `extdeps.cloud.gcp.errors`' `GcpRpcCodeOther` and
// `extdeps.container.oci.types`' `OciMediaTypeOther` are written the same way, outside this file.
//
// Section 6b's trigger is the second local implementation, so the generalization is overdue, and part of
// it is taken HERE: what the six genuinely share is the CHECK, and the check is now one declaration,
// `openai_documented_wire_name`, which this member routes through and which any migration should adopt.
// What is not folded together is the documented-name TABLES, and the reason holds rather than being
// convenient: they are six different upstream enumerations from three different endpoints, each with its
// own source, so they are not six copies of one fact -- one table over a type parameter (the parametric
// precedents are `std.algebra`'s `Magma` and `std.affine_space`'s `SpatialResult`) would still need six
// row-sets supplied per member and its unknown-name behaviour, and that shape is not yet read off a
// second use. Migrating them is also not a local edit: a parse's return type is reader-visible, and all
// five are called by `test/claim/extdeps_llm_type_grounding_witness`, which has to be carried member by
// member. So the follow-up is declared with its trigger in `openai_chat_completion_wire_frontier_rows`,
// not assumed away.
//
// THE DOCUMENTED SET IS SEVEN VALUES, NOT FOUR: none, minimal, low, medium, high, xhigh, max. The four-arm
// version of this type could not represent a valid request that asks for `xhigh`, which is the same class
// of defect as making an optional request member required -- a real caller's message had no inhabitant. The
// names are the upstream ones, read off the generated `ReasoningEffort` alias under the anchor at the top of
// this file; `extdeps.openrouter` already carries all seven, so this is not a set invented here either.
//
// AN UNDOCUMENTED NAME STAYS WHOLE, AND AN EMPTY NAME REFUSES THE PARSE. A name outside the seven is the
// endpoint's knowledge, not this module's, so it is kept rather than folded into a nearest guess -- but it
// is kept through the checked constructor, so `""` yields Absent instead of a carrier whose type promises
// non-empty. That refusal belongs to this endpoint's wire, and the general law stays `std.types`'
// `string_non_empty`, which the constructor calls.
type OpenAiReasoningEffort
  = OpenAiReasoningEffortNone
  | OpenAiReasoningEffortMinimal
  | OpenAiReasoningEffortLow
  | OpenAiReasoningEffortMedium
  | OpenAiReasoningEffortHigh
  | OpenAiReasoningEffortXHigh
  | OpenAiReasoningEffortMax
  | OpenAiReasoningEffortUndocumented { raw: NonEmptyStr }

data openai_reasoning_effort_none_wire: String = "none"
data openai_reasoning_effort_minimal_wire: String = "minimal"
data openai_reasoning_effort_low_wire: String = "low"
data openai_reasoning_effort_medium_wire: String = "medium"
data openai_reasoning_effort_high_wire: String = "high"
data openai_reasoning_effort_xhigh_wire: String = "xhigh"
data openai_reasoning_effort_max_wire: String = "max"

// THE ONE CHECK THE SIX COPIES SHARE. A wire name is carried as `NonEmptyStr`, and that predicate is
// enforced at literal sites only until compile-time evaluation of where-predicates lands, so assigning a
// runtime `String` into the field -- which is what all five older copies do -- checks nothing. One checked
// constructor owns the decision instead: Present when the name has a character, Absent when it does not,
// with no default and no sanitizing. `std.types`' `string_non_empty` is the law; this is the call site.
fn openai_documented_wire_name(raw: String) -> NonEmptyStr? {
  if string_non_empty(value: raw) {
    Present { value: raw as NonEmptyStr }
  } else {
    Absent
  }
}

// Wire name in, variant out -- or Absent, for a name with no characters in it. A request that names an
// eighth effort is not silently read as one of the seven, and it is not refused here either: the endpoint
// owns the answer to an effort it does not know, and this model reports the shape.
fn parse_openai_reasoning_effort(raw: String) -> OpenAiReasoningEffort? {
  if raw == openai_reasoning_effort_none_wire { Present { value: OpenAiReasoningEffortNone } }
  else if raw == openai_reasoning_effort_minimal_wire { Present { value: OpenAiReasoningEffortMinimal } }
  else if raw == openai_reasoning_effort_low_wire { Present { value: OpenAiReasoningEffortLow } }
  else if raw == openai_reasoning_effort_medium_wire { Present { value: OpenAiReasoningEffortMedium } }
  else if raw == openai_reasoning_effort_high_wire { Present { value: OpenAiReasoningEffortHigh } }
  else if raw == openai_reasoning_effort_xhigh_wire { Present { value: OpenAiReasoningEffortXHigh } }
  else if raw == openai_reasoning_effort_max_wire { Present { value: OpenAiReasoningEffortMax } }
  else {
    match openai_documented_wire_name(raw: raw) {
      Present { value: name } => Present { value: OpenAiReasoningEffortUndocumented { raw: name } }
      Absent => Absent
    }
  }
}

fn openai_reasoning_effort_wire(effort: OpenAiReasoningEffort) -> String {
  match effort {
    OpenAiReasoningEffortNone => openai_reasoning_effort_none_wire
    OpenAiReasoningEffortMinimal => openai_reasoning_effort_minimal_wire
    OpenAiReasoningEffortLow => openai_reasoning_effort_low_wire
    OpenAiReasoningEffortMedium => openai_reasoning_effort_medium_wire
    OpenAiReasoningEffortHigh => openai_reasoning_effort_high_wire
    OpenAiReasoningEffortXHigh => openai_reasoning_effort_xhigh_wire
    OpenAiReasoningEffortMax => openai_reasoning_effort_max_wire
    OpenAiReasoningEffortUndocumented { raw: r } => r
  }
}

// ONE EVENT PAYLOAD of a streamed answer. The delta is what changed since the previous event: the
// first event usually carries a role and no content, a middle event carries content and no role,
// the last carries a finish_reason and neither. So every delta member is optional, and absent is
// not empty -- an empty `content` is a token that is the empty string, which is a different fact
// from a chunk that sent no content member at all.
data openai_chat_completion_chunk_object_wire: String = "chat.completion.chunk"

// THE CHUNK'S `object` IS A CONSTANT IN THE SPEC, SO IT IS TYPED AS ONE AND BUILT ONLY BY CHECKING --
// the same shape as `OpenAiTextCompletionObject`, and for the same reason: the chat answer, the chunk and
// a text completion all carry an `object` member, and while its member type was `String` a reader could
// hand a `text_completion` or an error envelope to anything expecting a chunk. A nominal carrier plus a
// constructor that yields Present for the documented value and Absent for everything else is DESIGN
// section 4's `gunbc.design_ruling` where_refinements_retire_for_checked_constructors; the where-BRAND
// carries identity only (the atom yields a `WherePredicateMarker`, never evaluated as a refinement), so
// the type claims nothing the compiler cannot hold. Pattern: `extdeps.languages.json.grammar`'s
// `JsonNumberLexeme` with `json_number_lexeme_valid`, `json_number_lexeme_unchecked` and the constructor
// `json_number_lexeme`.
type OpenAiChatCompletionChunkObject = String where brand("OpenAiChatCompletionChunkObject")

fn openai_chat_completion_chunk_object_valid(s: String) -> Bool {
  s == openai_chat_completion_chunk_object_wire
}

// The coercion is separate so the checked constructor stays the only producer of a carrier in this
// repository. That is a claim about call sites, not reachability: `dag` has no visibility modifier, so
// nothing hides this, and what the brand does prevent is a raw String standing in for the carrier.
fn openai_chat_completion_chunk_object_unchecked(s: String) -> OpenAiChatCompletionChunkObject {
  s as OpenAiChatCompletionChunkObject
}

// Present for "chat.completion.chunk", Absent for everything else -- including "text_completion", the
// chat answer's "chat.completion" and any error envelope.
fn openai_chat_completion_chunk_object(s: String) -> OpenAiChatCompletionChunkObject? {
  if openai_chat_completion_chunk_object_valid(s: s) {
    Present { value: openai_chat_completion_chunk_object_unchecked(s: s) }
  } else {
    Absent
  }
}

type OpenAiChatCompletionChunkDelta {
  role: OpenAiChatMessageRole?
  content: String?
  refusal: String?
}

type OpenAiChatCompletionChunkChoice {
  index: Int
  delta: OpenAiChatCompletionChunkDelta
  logprobs: OpenAiChatCompletion200Logprobs?
  finish_reason: OpenAiFinishReason?
}

type OpenAiChatCompletionChunkBody {
  id: String
  object: OpenAiChatCompletionChunkObject
  created: Int
  model: String
  choices: List<OpenAiChatCompletionChunkChoice>
  usage: OpenAiChatCompletion200Usage?
  service_tier: String?
  system_fingerprint: String?
}

// A streamed chunk's tool-call deltas are PARTIAL: an event may carry only a call index and a
// fragment of one argument string, with no id and no function name, so the ToolCall record above
// (id, type, function) cannot hold one. Modelling the accumulation is its own change: it needs a
// decision about where the partial call is held between events, which belongs with whoever reads
// the stream, not with the wire shape. Declared here rather than papered over with optional
// fields on ToolCall, which would let a non-streaming request carry a half call.
data structural_coverage_gap_openai_chat_chunk_tool_call_deltas: List<CoverageClosureEntry> = [
  {
    facts: [
      Subject { path: "OpenAiChatCompletionChunkDelta" },
      Missing { item: "tool_call_delta_with_index_and_argument_fragment" },
      Missing { item: "function_call_delta" },
      Missing { item: "audio_delta" },
      Missing { item: "refusal_delta_annotation" }
    ],
    trigger: "a named home for a partial tool call held across events, with its accumulation rule"
  }
  {
    facts: [
      Subject { path: "OpenAiChatCompletionChunkBody" },
      Missing { item: "obfuscation" },
      Missing { item: "moderation" }
    ],
    trigger: "the first reader that must forward or act on what a chunk carries beyond content and usage -- obfuscation is sent by default whenever stream_options.include_obfuscation is not turned off, and moderation appears when the endpoint's moderation pass runs"
  }
]

// `OpenAiFinishReason` carries stop, length, tool_calls and content_filter. The generated `Choice` for
// this endpoint documents FIVE values, the fifth being the legacy `function_call`, so a response from a
// call that used the deprecated `functions` parameter has no inhabitant today. The gap is declared rather
// than closed here for a specific reason: the arms of this coproduct are top-level names in this module, so
// `FunctionCall` is taken by the record that holds a tool call's name and arguments, and the wire spelling
// is not free either -- `extdeps.llm.openai_contracts`' `openai_finish_reason_wire_contract` encodes this
// coproduct by `CoproductWireContract` with `StringVariant { naming: SnakeCase }`, so an arm named anything
// but `FunctionCall` would re-emit the wrong string, and `extdeps.llm.openai_rest` decodes the member
// through that contract today. Closing it means giving the member an explicit-name contract or renaming the
// colliding record, which is that contract's change to make with its readers, not this wire model's to
// guess at.
data structural_coverage_gap_openai_chat_finish_reason_function_call: List<CoverageClosureEntry> = [
  {
    facts: [
      Subject { path: "OpenAiFinishReason" },
      Missing { item: "function_call" }
    ],
    trigger: "the PR that gives openai_finish_reason_wire_contract per-variant wire names, or renames the FunctionCall record out of the collision, and carries extdeps.llm.openai_rest's decode of the member"
  }
]

// The request members this model does not carry, from the same anchor. Each is a member a caller
// may send today; a caller that sends one is not thereby malformed. They are declared missing
// rather than omitted, so the next change that needs one extends this record instead of
// re-reading the endpoint's shape somewhere else.
data structural_coverage_gap_openai_chat_completion_request_members: List<CoverageClosureEntry> = [
  {
    facts: [
      Subject { path: "OpenAiChatCompletionRequest" },
      Missing { item: "logit_bias" },
      Missing { item: "logprobs_and_top_logprobs" },
      Missing { item: "response_format" },
      Missing { item: "tools_tool_choice_parallel_tool_calls" },
      Missing { item: "legacy_functions_and_function_call" },
      Missing { item: "audio" },
      Missing { item: "modalities" },
      Missing { item: "prediction" },
      Missing { item: "service_tier" },
      Missing { item: "store_and_metadata" },
      Missing { item: "safety_identifier_and_user" },
      Missing { item: "web_search_options" },
      Missing { item: "prompt_cache_key" },
      Missing { item: "prompt_cache_options" },
      Missing { item: "prompt_cache_retention" },
      Missing { item: "verbosity" },
      Missing { item: "moderation" },
      Missing { item: "ttl_and_metadata" }
    ],
    trigger: "the first member a serving call must read or forward beyond sampling -- tools and response_format before the rest"
  }
]

// A sampling parameter is carried as an un-evaluated JSON number lexeme. That is a frontier, not
// a design: it dissolves when the language rules a float literal and operator home, at which
// point these four fields become numbers and any read that compares them becomes meaningful.
data openai_chat_completion_wire_frontier_rows: List<FrontierRow> = [
  frontier_row_decl(
    ref: decl_ref(module_path: "extdeps.llm.openai", decl_name: "OpenAiChatCompletionRequest"),
    reason: "temperature, top_p, presence_penalty and frequency_penalty are carried as extdeps.languages.json.grammar's JsonNumberLexeme, built only through its checked constructor json_number_lexeme, because std.float declares Float as a name with no operators and no ruled literal home (v2 refuses a float literal: infer_reason_float_literal_home_unruled), and the json parser never evaluates a number's lexeme. Nothing here range-checks or orders them: that would be validation on text standing in for a number",
    dissolution: unbound_dissolution(description: "feature:std-float-literal-and-operator-home - std.float rules a float literal home and the comparison operators for it, and extdeps.languages.json reads a lexeme into that value; then these four members are typed as that value, a read that rejects an out-of-range sampling parameter becomes meaningful and is placed at the caller that owns the range, and this row deletes. The lexeme path stays for a forwarder that must re-emit the client's bytes unchanged"),
  ),
  // The request record has no reader yet. Its consumer is named rather than assumed: the request
  // read of the serving path, which the approved plan dag/gunbc/plans/fabric_serving_router.dag
  // puts in its S3 decisions (model, stream, stop and reasoning_effort are exactly what that read
  // needs), and the dashboard client that sends the call. The row exists so an unread model is
  // tracked as debt (DESIGN section 3c) instead of being deleted quietly when the read lands.
  frontier_row_decl(
    ref: decl_ref(module_path: "extdeps.llm.openai", decl_name: "OpenAiChatCompletionRequest"),
    reason: "no module reads this record yet: the only consumer today is its own witness, and a model nobody reads is not yet evidence that the shape is right",
    dissolution: unbound_dissolution(description: "feature:s3-serving-request-read - the serving path's request read, which the approved plan gunbc.plans.fabric_serving_router puts in its S3 decisions, reads model, stream, stop and reasoning_effort out of this record, and the dashboard client builds it for the call it sends. It dissolves when that reader lands WITH a witness that builds a request of this shape and reads it back, so the record is paid for by an observation and not by a compile. The read belongs to that plan, not to this module: nothing here decides what to do with a request"),
  ),
  // The repeated enumerated-member pair, declared as debt with its carrier named rather than left
  // in a comment: §6b allows deferring a generalization only with a stated reason and trigger.
  frontier_row_decl(
    ref: decl_ref(module_path: "extdeps.llm.openai", decl_name: "OpenAiReasoningEffort"),
    reason: "the wire-name pair (table, read chain, unknown-keeping arm, re-emitting match) is written out by hand for the sixth time in this module, and the five older copies are the same shape -- Other { raw: NonEmptyStr } filled straight from a String, which is why the empty-name check now lives in one shared checked constructor, openai_documented_wire_name, instead of a hand-written guard per member. What is still six copies is the documented-name TABLE, and DESIGN section 6b's trigger for generalizing that was the second local implementation, so it is overdue: the reason it is deferred, and the fact that the idiom also stands in extdeps.cloud.gcp.errors and extdeps.container.oci.types, is in the comment above OpenAiReasoningEffort",
    dissolution: unbound_dissolution(description: "feature:openai-wire-name-table-generalization - one wire-name table over a type parameter (parametric declarations exist: std.algebra's Magma and std.affine_space's SpatialResult) taking each member's rows plus its unknown-name behaviour, adopted by all six members of this module and then by the same idiom in extdeps.cloud.gcp.errors and extdeps.container.oci.types. The migrating PR carries the readers with it member by member, which is where the cost really is: the five older parse functions are called by test/claim/extdeps_llm_type_grounding_witness, and a parse's return type is reader-visible"),
  ),
  // Same for the streamed payload: the framing is already read by extdeps.llm.openai_compat_sse,
  // but nothing yet reads what one of those events carries.
  frontier_row_decl(
    ref: decl_ref(module_path: "extdeps.llm.openai", decl_name: "OpenAiChatCompletionChunkBody"),
    reason: "no module reads one chunk payload yet; openai_compat_sse frames the events and this record describes their content, and the two are only joined by a reader",
    dissolution: unbound_dissolution(description: "feature:s3-streamed-answer-read - the serving path's streamed read named in the approved plan gunbc.plans.fabric_serving_router's S3 decisions forwards one payload of this shape and closes the usage record at stream end. It dissolves when that reader lands WITH a witness that decodes a recorded chat.completion.chunk -- the role-only first event, a content delta, and the finish_reason-only last event -- into this record"),
  ),
]

// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
// THE LEGACY TEXT COMPLETIONS ENDPOINT, /v1/completions. The chat endpoint above is the one most
// callers reach for; this one is served alongside it by the engines the rented cards run, and the
// model is not "chat minus messages" -- the prompt is a union of four shapes, three members exist
// only here (suffix, echo, best_of), and a choice carries a string where a chat choice carries a
// message or a delta. Its authority is its own anchor below: the two endpoints are documented and
// versioned separately, and borrowing the chat anchor would let a change to one silently claim
// authority over the other. Read 2026-11-01.
data extdeps_completions_external_authority_anchor: ExternalAuthority = ExternalAuthority {
  uri: Uri {
    scheme: Https
    locator: "platform.openai.com/docs/api-reference/completions/create"
  }
}

// Both this endpoint's answer shapes name themselves with this literal, streamed and not, and it is
// NOT the chat chunk's literal: a reader that branches on `object` must not be able to confuse a
// whole text-completion answer with one event of a streamed chat answer.
data openai_text_completion_object_wire: String = "text_completion"

// THE `object` MEMBER IS A CONSTANT IN THE SPEC, SO IT IS TYPED AS ONE, AND IT IS CONSTRUCTED ONLY BY
// CHECKING. The two text-completion bodies used to type `object: String`, which made the endpoints
// indistinguishable at the type: a `chat.completion`, a `chat.completion.chunk` and an error envelope
// would each have type-checked as a text completion, and the constant above stood nowhere near the
// fields it describes. It is now a carrier with a checked constructor, so a decoder can obtain the
// value for one endpoint and refuse every other one:
//
//   extdeps.languages.json.grammar is the pattern: its `JsonNumberLexeme` carrier is declared as
//   `String where brand("JsonNumberLexeme")` alongside `json_number_lexeme_valid`, the
//   `json_number_lexeme_unchecked` coercion, and the checked constructor `json_number_lexeme` returning
//   Optional. A where-BRAND carries nominal identity only -- `std.types`' `brand` yields a
//   `WherePredicateMarker`, which is never evaluated as a refinement -- so no validation is claimed by
//   the type: the check lives in the constructor, which is DESIGN section 4's ruling
//   gunbc.design_ruling where_refinements_retire_for_checked_constructors -- "where-refinements are
//   retired in favour of checked constructors returning `Optional`". That is why this is not spelled
//   `String where openai_text_completion_object_is_documented`: `std.types`' `NonEmptyStr` is still
//   spelled that way, but it is the legacy that ruling retires, not a pattern to copy, and DESIGN
//   section 4 also refuses to lean on `gunbc.design_ruling`'s
//   `literal_only_refinement_judgment_is_interim`, an explicitly interim judgment, for a value that
//   arrives from a decoder rather than being written in source.
//
// The refusal is a refusal, not a default: no arm of this constructor yields a carrier for a value that
// is not the documented constant, so a body from another endpoint cannot be laundered into a text
// completion (§5). The consumer is executed in-repo today:
// //test/claim/extdeps/openai_text_completion_wire_witness calls the constructor with the documented
// value (Present) and with each chat endpoint's value (Absent), so a constant that drifted goes red.
type OpenAiTextCompletionObject = String where brand("OpenAiTextCompletionObject")

fn openai_text_completion_object_valid(s: String) -> Bool {
  s == openai_text_completion_object_wire
}

// The coercion is spelled separately, following `json_number_lexeme_unchecked`, so that the checked
// constructor below is the only thing in THIS REPOSITORY that produces a carrier. That is a claim about
// call sites, not reachability: the language has no visibility modifier anywhere in `dag`, so nothing
// hides this -- what a caller cannot do is substitute a raw String where the carrier is expected, because
// that identity is exactly what the where-brand carries.
fn openai_text_completion_object_unchecked(s: String) -> OpenAiTextCompletionObject {
  s as OpenAiTextCompletionObject
}

// Present for "text_completion", Absent for anything else -- including "chat.completion" and
// "chat.completion.chunk", which is what stops a chat answer or an error envelope from reading as a text
// completion.
fn openai_text_completion_object(s: String) -> OpenAiTextCompletionObject? {
  if openai_text_completion_object_valid(s: s) {
    Present { value: openai_text_completion_object_unchecked(s: s) }
  } else {
    Absent
  }
}

// The prompt member as the endpoint gives it. Four arms, each cited to the one member's union in the
// anchors at the top of this file: the docs page (member `completions-prompt`) for the meaning, and the
// vendor's generated `CompletionCreateParams.prompt` for the shape --
// `Union[str, Sequence[str], Iterable[int], Iterable[Iterable[int]], None]` -- which lists exactly these
// four shapes and no others:
//   PromptText       -- string             one prompt, one completion
//   PromptTexts      -- array<string>      one completion per entry
//   PromptTokens     -- array<int>         one prompt, already tokenized by the caller
//   PromptTokenLists -- array<array<int>>  several tokenized prompts
// A coproduct rather than a String field, because a String folds the four together and loses the
// difference between one prompt containing a comma and two prompts -- which is the difference between
// one completion and two, so it is not a detail a reader can recover. Tokens stay integers here: they
// are already the engine's own vocabulary, and re-rendering them as text would make the tokenizer's
// decision a routing fact.
//
// THE MEMBER IS REQUIRED, SO IT IS NOT AN OPTION HERE. The docs page lists `completions-prompt` as
// required with no default, and the vendor's generated parameter says the same in code:
// `prompt: Required[Union[str, SequenceNotStr[str], Iterable[int], Iterable[Iterable[int]], None]]` --
// `SequenceNotStr` is upstream's own guard against reading a bare string as a list of characters, and it
// is the reason `PromptTexts` is a list of strings and not a list of anything.. A request
// record that typed this as `OpenAiCompletionPrompt?` would let a caller build a request the upstream
// contract refuses -- for a REQUEST record, faithfulness means required members are not optional, and a
// state that cannot legally occur is not a case this type should carry.
//
// The generated union also admits `None`, which is not the same thing as being absent: it is the member
// present and holding null. That is deliberately not an arm here either. A null prompt asks for nothing to
// complete, and the endpoint refuses it; four shapes are the four things a caller can actually ask for.
type OpenAiCompletionPrompt
  = PromptText { text: String }
  | PromptTexts { texts: List<String> }
  | PromptTokens { tokens: List<Int> }
  | PromptTokenLists { token_lists: List<List<Int>> }

// The sampling members are the same carrier as the chat request's, for the same reason: std.float has no
// ruled literal or operator home, the carrier is `extdeps.languages.json.grammar`'s `JsonNumberLexeme`
// built only through `json_number_lexeme`, and nothing here compares or range-checks them. `JsonNumber`
// itself is a VARIANT of `extdeps.languages.json.emit`'s `JsonValue`, not a type a field may be typed as.
// `openai_chat_completion_wire_frontier_rows` carries that frontier for both endpoints' requests; a ruled
// float home dissolves one row, not one per endpoint.
type OpenAiTextCompletionRequest {
  model: String
  prompt: OpenAiCompletionPrompt
  suffix: String?
  max_tokens: Int?
  best_of: Int?
  echo: Bool?
  n: Int?
  seed: Int?
  stop: OpenAiCompletionStop?
  // Optional here for the same reason it is optional on the chat request: the generated parameters carry
  // it as two overloads, `Optional[Literal[False]]` and `Required[Literal[True]]`, so a client that never
  // mentions `stream` is sending a valid request that a required `Bool` would make unrepresentable. Absent
  // is read as "not streaming", which is upstream's meaning and is stated rather than defaulted.
  stream: Bool?
  stream_options: OpenAiStreamOptions?
  temperature: JsonNumberLexeme?
  top_p: JsonNumberLexeme?
  presence_penalty: JsonNumberLexeme?
  frequency_penalty: JsonNumberLexeme?
}

type OpenAiTextCompletionChoice {
  index: Int
  text: String
  finish_reason: OpenAiFinishReason?
}

// `usage` is the chat record, reused. The two endpoint documents give that member the same shape and
// the same members, so a second record with the same fields would put one fact in two places and let
// them drift while both claimed to describe usage. `choices` is deliberately NOT shared: here a choice
// is a string, there it is a message.
type OpenAiTextCompletion200Body {
  id: String
  object: OpenAiTextCompletionObject
  created: Int
  model: String
  choices: List<OpenAiTextCompletionChoice>
  usage: OpenAiChatCompletion200Usage?
  service_tier: String?
  system_fingerprint: String?
}

// One event of a streamed answer from this endpoint. Two facts a reader needs and cannot infer from
// the non-streaming shape: the final event carries a finish_reason and NO text, so `text` is optional
// here while it is required above; and an engine may send a closing frame with usage and an empty
// choices list, so `choices` is a list that may be empty rather than a non-empty one.
type OpenAiTextCompletionChunkChoice {
  index: Int
  text: String?
  finish_reason: OpenAiFinishReason?
}

type OpenAiTextCompletionChunkBody {
  id: String
  object: OpenAiTextCompletionObject
  created: Int
  model: String
  choices: List<OpenAiTextCompletionChunkChoice>
  usage: OpenAiChatCompletion200Usage?
}

data structural_coverage_gap_openai_text_completion_members: List<CoverageClosureEntry> = [
  {
    facts: [
      Subject { path: "OpenAiTextCompletionRequest" },
      Missing { item: "logit_bias" },
      Missing { item: "logprobs" },
      Missing { item: "user" }
    ],
    trigger: "the first member a serving call must forward on this endpoint beyond sampling -- logprobs before the rest, since it is the one that cannot be recovered after the answer arrives"
  },
  {
    facts: [
      Subject { path: "OpenAiTextCompletionChoice" },
      Missing { item: "logprobs_token_ranks" }
    ],
    trigger: "a reader that prices or explains a completion by token rank; the chat side's OpenAiChatCompletion200Logprobs is the shape to compare against before inventing a second one"
  },
  {
    facts: [
      Subject { path: "OpenAiTextCompletionChunkChoice" },
      Missing { item: "logprobs_token_ranks" }
    ],
    trigger: "the streamed counterpart of the row above, which needs the accumulation rule for per-token logprobs across events"
  },
  {
    facts: [
      Subject { path: "OpenAiTextCompletionChoice" },
      Missing { item: "finish_reason_is_the_chat_endpoint's_wider_set" }
    ],
    trigger: "a text-completion finish_reason of its own. The generated CompletionChoice documents exactly stop, length and content_filter for this endpoint, so typing the member with the chat coproduct OpenAiFinishReason admits values (tool_calls, and function_call once that gap closes) this endpoint never sends -- a superset, which is a reader's trap rather than a lie. A separate coproduct is blocked in this module by name, not by meaning: its unit arms would have to be Stop, Length and ContentFilter, and those three are already OpenAiFinishReason's arms, whose wire spelling comes from openai_finish_reason_wire_contract. The PR that gives this endpoint its own finish_reason either declares it in another module or gives both coproducts per-variant wire names"
  }
]

// No module reads the text-completion shapes yet, and the consumer is named rather than assumed: the
// same serving-path read that the approved plan gunbc.plans.fabric_serving_router puts in its S3
// decisions, on whichever endpoint the client called. Tracked as debt (DESIGN section 3c) so an unread
// model cannot be deleted quietly, and so its absence is visible rather than implied by the endpoint
// existing.
data openai_text_completion_wire_frontier_rows: List<FrontierRow> = [
  frontier_row_decl(
    ref: decl_ref(module_path: "extdeps.llm.openai", decl_name: "OpenAiTextCompletionRequest"),
    reason: "no module builds or reads this record yet: its only consumer is the naming of it in this module's own coverage rows",
    dissolution: unbound_dissolution(description: "feature:s3-completions-request-read - the serving path's request read in the approved plan gunbc.plans.fabric_serving_router's S3 decisions, on the /v1/completions endpoint: it reads this record's model, stream, prompt shape and stop, and a client builds the record for the call it sends. It dissolves when that reader lands WITH a witness that builds a request of this shape and reads it back. The decisions about a request belong to that plan, not here"),
  ),
  frontier_row_decl(
    ref: decl_ref(module_path: "extdeps.llm.openai", decl_name: "OpenAiTextCompletion200Body"),
    reason: "no module reads a non-streaming text-completion answer yet, and none refuses a body whose `object` member is not the documented constant",
    dissolution: unbound_dissolution(description: "feature:s3-completions-answer-read - the serving path's read in the approved plan gunbc.plans.fabric_serving_router's S3 decisions closes a usage record from one body of this shape. It dissolves when that reader lands WITH a witness that decodes a recorded completions 200 body into this record and asserts its choices and usage, so a shape nobody has fed real bytes through is not carried as truth"),
  ),
  frontier_row_decl(
    ref: decl_ref(module_path: "extdeps.llm.openai", decl_name: "OpenAiTextCompletionChunkBody"),
    reason: "no module reads one streamed text-completion event yet, and none refuses a payload whose `object` member is not the documented constant; openai_compat_sse frames such events but does not interpret their content",
    dissolution: unbound_dissolution(description: "feature:s3-completions-chunk-read - the serving path's streamed read in the approved plan gunbc.plans.fabric_serving_router's S3 decisions forwards one payload of this shape and finishes the answer at the sentinel. It dissolves when that reader lands WITH a witness that decodes a recorded completions chunk into this record -- including the final event, which carries a finish_reason and no text"),
  ),
  frontier_row_decl(
    ref: decl_ref(module_path: "extdeps.llm.openai", decl_name: "structural_coverage_gap_openai_text_completion_members"),
    reason: "no module reads this coverage list; it is written by this module's own convention and read by nothing, as are its predecessors structural_coverage_gap_openai_chat_completion_200_residual and structural_coverage_gap_openai_chat_completion_request_members",
    dissolution: unbound_dissolution(description: "feature:coverage-closure-rollup - a roll-up that reads each extdeps module's structural_coverage_gap_* lists into one census view retires this row together with the unread siblings it names, in this module and in the other extdeps modules written the same way. Checked rather than assumed: no consumer of extdeps.coverage's CoverageClosureEntry type exists in `dag` outside the declaring modules, and the seed's declaration_index roster names such a list only where its entries are cited-field debt"),
  )
]
